  "cta": "Send this to someone who invests"
 },
 "caption_en": "One of these three stocks never fell more than 15% in 63 years. Guess which before the end.\n\nIf countries were stocks: GDP per person, current US$, World Bank, 1960 to 2025.\n\nStock A: $718 in 1960. Oil boom: $28,703 in 1981 (40x in 21 years). Bust: $9,166 by 1988 (down 68%). Back above the 1981 peak only in 2012. 2025: $34,537.\nStock B: $156 in 1960, $3,086 in 2025.\nStock C: $1,452 in 1960. Since 1962, never down more than 15% (worst: 1983 to 1985, down 14%). 2025: $60,337.\n\nStock A grew the most in percent. Stock C ends highest.\n\nThe reveal: A is Saudi Arabia. B is Egypt. C, with almost no oil or gas income (natural resource rents 0.4% of GDP, 2021), is Israel.\n\nNo oil isn't the secret on its own: Jordan (0.1%) and Lebanon (0.0%) have almost none either.\n\nCurrent US$, not adjusted for inflation or prices. Not a stock, not a forecast, not financial advice.\n\nSources: World Bank, World Development Indicators: GDP per capita (current US$, NY.GDP.PCAP.CD) and total natural resource rents (% of GDP, NY.GDP.TOTL.RT.ZS), accessed Nov 2026. Photos: Khurais oil field, Planet Labs, CC BY-SA 4.0; Intel Kiryat Gat, Kiryat Gat archive, CC BY 2.5; Hatzeva, Negev 1971, Moshe Milner, GPO (PD). Made with AI tools, AI voice (Noam's cloned voice), follow line in Noam's own voice.",
 "caption_he": "3 מניות מסתוריות. 65 שנה. באיזו הייתם בוחרים?\nהתמ\"ג לנפש (הבנק העולמי, דולרים שוטפים):\nמניה A: 718 דולר ב-1960, 28,703 ב-1981, ואז קריסה של 68% עד 1988. רק ב-2012 חזרה לשיא. היום 34,537.\nמניה B: 156 דולר ב-1960, 3,086 היום.\nמניה C: 1,452 דולר ב-1960. מאז 1962 אף פעם לא ירדה ביותר מ-15%. היום 60,337.\nA היא סעודיה. B היא מצרים. C, כמעט בלי הכנסות מנפט וגז, היא ישראל.\nלא מניה, לא תחזית, לא ייעוץ השקעות.",
